IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- the rates of income tax on an individual (s 3 "tax-free threshold",
-- "prescribed non-resident", "resident taxpayer", "ordinary taxable income"; s 12(1); Schedule 7 Part I clauses 1 and 4, Part II
-- clauses 1 and 4, Part III), the part-year residency period (ss 16, 18, 20(1)), and the rates on a company (s 23(2), (6);
-- s 23AA "base rate entity").
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 66, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 50, 2026 (Register id
-- C2026C00300), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03348.txt. The deposit drops every formula that was set as
-- an image ("in accordance with the following formula:" is followed by nothing), including s 20's pro-rating formula and
-- Schedule 7 clauses 2 and 3.
--
-- DATED ARM FOR 2023-24 (REQ-0056, 22 October 2026). Compilation No. 62, compilation date 1 April 2024, includes amendments up
-- to Act No. 3, 2024 (Register id C2024C00132), the compilation in force at the end of the 2023-24 year of income, as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03348.2024-04-01.txt. Its Schedule 7 Parts I, II and III each have a table
-- "for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income"; they are added below and used for 2023-24 only (Compilation
-- No. 62 is not the compilation that was in force for the earlier years it names). The other provisions encoded here read the
-- same in both compilations, except s 16 "eligible pensioner" (c), which in Compilation No. 62 reads "other than Part 2.11,
-- 2.12, 2.15 or 3.15A": a 2023-24 payment under Part 3.15A is not modelled (no field tells it apart; NOTES.md).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0019 in ../../../requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 3 times by the Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave scenarios: chloe c045 (2024-10-20, first tax return for 2023-24, taxable income $27,500), chloe c048
-- (2025-10-25, second return for 2024-25, taxable income $71,500) and daniel d04a (2033-11-30, Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty
-- Ltd's first company return: "What rate"). SCOPED to the provisions the lives cite (Schedule 7; s 23 base rate entity), with
-- the definitions, residency tests, the superannuation and employment-termination remainders and the working holiday maker
-- rules that change the Schedule 7 answer.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Schedule 7 clauses 2 and 3 (abnormal income averaging; formula not in the deposit); the pro-rating formula in
-- s 20 (not in the deposit -- the pro-rated threshold is an INPUT); ss 12(4)-(13), 12AA, 12A, 13-15 (trustees, primary
-- producers, minors' income under Div 6AA); Schedules 8 to 12; s 23(3)-(5), (7), 23A and ss 25-30 (RSA providers, PDFs, credit
-- unions, life insurers, trusts, super funds, sovereign entities); s 23AB's list of passive income (base rate entity passive
-- income is an INPUT). Tax offsets (the low income tax offset), the Medicare levy and HELP repayments are other Acts.
-- Where a rule can reach one of these gaps it answers `not covered`, naming the gap; see `Why not covered` below.
--
-- A year of income is named by the calendar year in which it begins: 2024 is the 2024-25 year of income. Amounts are
-- Australian dollars.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, written with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC USE. See NOTES.md.
-- Conformed to the writing-l4-rules skill on 14 October 2026, and to section 5 of docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md (what the stable l4,
-- 1.6.98, accepts) on 22 October 2026. Edit this file directly; the generator that first laid it out is retired.

§ `Income Tax Rates Act 1986 -- rates`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A rule that can reach a gap answers with an `Answer`: either `answered` with the value, or
-- `not covered` with the reason, which is one of these. Each reason is the message the first pass gave its named refusal.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- Schedule 7: Compilation No. 66 has tables from 2024-25; Compilation No. 62 is used for 2023-24 (REQ-0056)
    `the deposited compilations have no Schedule 7 table for a year of income before 2023-24`
    -- Schedule 7 Parts I and II clauses 2 and 3: the formula is an image the deposit dropped
    `Schedule 7 clauses 2 and 3 (a special income component) are not encoded: their formula is not in the deposited compilation`
    -- s 20(1): the formula is an image the deposit dropped
    `the s 20(1) formula is not in the deposited compilation, and no pro-rated tax-free threshold was supplied`
    -- s 23(2): no year of income stated; the encoder's boundary (NOTES.md finding 12)
    `this encoding states no company rate for a year of income before 2024-25`
    -- s 23(1); s 12(6) and Schedule 10 are not encoded
    `s 23 does not give the rate for a company in the capacity of a trustee, and the rate that does is not encoded`
    -- s 23(3)-(5), s 23A
    `the rates in s 23(3) to (5) and s 23A (RSA providers, PDFs, life insurance companies) are not encoded`
    -- s 23(7)
    `the s 23(7) ceiling for a recognised medium credit union is not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `s 3 -- the tax-free threshold`

-- s 3(1): "tax-free threshold means $18,200."
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 3(1), "tax-free threshold"
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax-free threshold` MEANS 18200

§§ `s 3 and s 16 -- the person, and the payments both definitions list`

-- s 3(1): "prescribed non-resident ... means a person who, at all times during the year of income, is a non-resident, not being
-- a person to whom, at any time during the year of income, compensation or a pension, allowance or benefit is payable under:
-- (a) the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986; ... (ba) the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004; or (c) the Social
-- Security Act 1991; being compensation or a pension, allowance or benefit in respect of which the person is liable to be
-- assessed and to pay income tax in Australia."
-- s 16: "eligible pensioner ... means a person to whom, at any time during the year of income, compensation or a pension,
-- allowance or benefit is payable under:" the same (a), (b) and (ba), and "(c) a provision of the Social Security Act 1991
-- other than Part 2.11, 2.12 or 2.15 of that Act", with the same "being ..." tail. The two lists differ ONLY in (c), so the
-- Social Security Act payment is split into the two kinds the lists tell apart.
-- Each field below means: compensation or a pension, allowance or benefit of that kind is payable to the person at some time
-- during the year of income, and the person is liable to be assessed and to pay income tax in Australia in respect of it.
DECLARE `Payments in the year of income` HAS
    `under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986`                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `under subsection 4(6) of the Veterans' Entitlements (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `under a provision of the Social Security Act 1991 other than Part 2.11, 2.12 or 2.15`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `under Part 2.11, 2.12 or 2.15 of the Social Security Act 1991`                                               IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 18(1) turns on when in the year the person commenced or ceased to be a resident. Months are months of the year of income:
-- 1 is July, 12 is June. A person who ceased and later commenced again in one year is not modelled (no constructor reaches it).
DECLARE `Residency in the year of income` IS ONE OF
    `a resident throughout the year`
    `a non-resident throughout the year`
    `ceased to be a resident during month`                 HAS `month ceased`    IS A NUMBER
    `commenced to be a resident during month`              HAS `month commenced` IS A NUMBER
    `commenced and later ceased to be a resident, months`  HAS `month commenced` IS A NUMBER
                                                               `month ceased`    IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Individual HAS
    `year of income begins`                               IS A NUMBER
    `residency`                                           IS A `Residency in the year of income`
    `payments`                                            IS A `Payments in the year of income`
    `pro-rated tax-free threshold`                        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `taxable income`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `superannuation remainder`                            IS A NUMBER
    `employment termination remainder`                    IS A NUMBER
    `working holiday taxable income`                      IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income includes a special income component`  IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `s 3 -- prescribed non-resident, resident taxpayer`

@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 3(1), "prescribed non-resident" (a)-(c)
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a payment listed in the definition of prescribed non-resident is payable to` `p` MEANS
        "(a)"  ... `p`'s `payments`'s `under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986`
    ..  "(b)"  ... `p`'s `payments`'s `under subsection 4(6) of the Veterans' Entitlements (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1986`
    ..  "(ba)" ... `p`'s `payments`'s `under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004`
    OR  "(c)"  ... `the Social Security Act 1991, any provision` `p`
    WHERE
        `the Social Security Act 1991, any provision` `q` MEANS
                `q`'s `payments`'s `under a provision of the Social Security Act 1991 other than Part 2.11, 2.12 or 2.15`
            OR  `q`'s `payments`'s `under Part 2.11, 2.12 or 2.15 of the Social Security Act 1991`

@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 3(1), "prescribed non-resident"
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a prescribed non-resident` `p` MEANS
        `p`'s `residency` EQUALS `a non-resident throughout the year`
    AND NOT (`a payment listed in the definition of prescribed non-resident is payable to` `p`)

-- s 3(1): "resident taxpayer ... means a taxpayer who is not a prescribed non-resident"; "non-resident taxpayer ... means a
-- taxpayer who is a prescribed non-resident".
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 3(1), "resident taxpayer"
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a resident taxpayer` `p` MEANS NOT (`a prescribed non-resident` `p`)

§§ `ss 16, 18, 20(1) -- part-year residency and the pro-rated threshold`

@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 16, "eligible pensioner" (a)-(c)
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an eligible pensioner` `p` MEANS
        "(a)"  ... `p`'s `payments`'s `under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986`
    ..  "(b)"  ... `p`'s `payments`'s `under subsection 4(6) of the Veterans' Entitlements (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1986`
    ..  "(ba)" ... `p`'s `payments`'s `under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004`
    OR  "(c)"  ... `p`'s `payments`'s `under a provision of the Social Security Act 1991 other than Part 2.11, 2.12 or 2.15`

DECLARE `Period of the year of income` HAS
    `from the beginning of month` IS A NUMBER
    `until the end of month`      IS A NUMBER

-- s 18(1): "(a) where the person was a resident at the beginning of the first month of the year of income and continued to be a
-- resident until a time during a subsequent month in the year of income when the person ceased to be a resident -- the period
-- from the beginning of the year of income until the end of that subsequent month; (b) where the person commenced to be a
-- resident during a month of the year of income and continued to be a resident until the end of the year of income -- the
-- period from the beginning of that month until the end of the year of income; (c) where the person commenced to be a resident
-- during a month of the year of income and continued to be a resident until a time during a subsequent month of the year of
-- income when the person ceased to be a resident -- the period from the beginning of that first-mentioned month until the end
-- of that subsequent month." The period, if any, before s 18(2) is applied.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 18(1)(a)-(c)
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of the year of income`
`the period described in s 18(1) for` `p` MEANS
    CONSIDER `p`'s `residency`
    WHEN `a resident throughout the year`     THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a non-resident throughout the year` THEN NOTHING
    -- (a): "a subsequent month" -- a month after the first
    WHEN `ceased to be a resident during month` `ceased`
        THEN IF   `ceased` AT LEAST 2
             THEN JUST (`Period of the year of income` OF 1, `ceased`)
             ELSE NOTHING
    -- (b)
    WHEN `commenced to be a resident during month` `commenced`
        THEN JUST (`Period of the year of income` OF `commenced`, 12)
    -- (c): "a subsequent month" -- a month after the month of commencement
    WHEN `commenced and later ceased to be a resident, months` `commenced` `ceased`
        THEN IF   `ceased` GREATER THAN `commenced`
             THEN JUST (`Period of the year of income` OF `commenced`, `ceased`)
             ELSE NOTHING

-- s 18(2): "A period shall not be taken to be a part-year residency period in relation to a person in relation to a year of
-- income if: (a) the person is an eligible pensioner in relation to the year of income; or (b) the period is the whole of the
-- year of income."
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 18(1), (2)
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`there is a part-year residency period for` `p` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period described in s 18(1) for` `p`
    WHEN NOTHING        THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `period`  THEN
                "(2)(a)" ... NOT (`an eligible pensioner` `p`)
            AND "(2)(b)" ... NOT (`the period is the whole of the year of income` `period`)
    WHERE
        `the period is the whole of the year of income` `q` MEANS
                `q`'s `from the beginning of month` EQUALS 1
            AND `q`'s `until the end of month`      EQUALS 12

-- s 20(1): the Schedule 7 Part I reference to the tax-free threshold is read "as if [it] were a reference to the amount
-- calculated in accordance with the following formula" -- THE FORMULA IS NOT IN THE DEPOSIT. The pro-rated threshold is an
-- INPUT here, and where a part-year residency period needs it and it was not supplied, the answer is `not covered`.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 20(1) -- the formula is an image the deposit dropped
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the tax-free threshold that applies to` `p` MEANS
    IF   `there is a part-year residency period for` `p`
    THEN CONSIDER `p`'s `pro-rated tax-free threshold`
         WHEN JUST `amount` THEN `answered` `amount`
         WHEN NOTHING       THEN `not covered` `the s 20(1) formula is not in the deposited compilation, and no pro-rated tax-free threshold was supplied`
    ELSE `answered` `the tax-free threshold`

§§ `s 3 -- ordinary taxable income`

-- s 3(1): "ordinary taxable income means the taxable income, reduced by the superannuation remainder of the taxable income and
-- by the employment termination remainder of the taxable income." (The remainders are the parts included under a maximum tax
-- rate provision in Divisions 301 and 82 of the 1997 Act that do not give rise to a tax offset: INPUTS here.)
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 3(1), "ordinary taxable income"
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ordinary taxable income of` `p` MEANS
          `p`'s `taxable income`
    MINUS `p`'s `superannuation remainder`
    MINUS `p`'s `employment termination remainder`

§§ `Schedule 7 -- the tables`

-- Every Schedule 7 table has the same three columns: "For the part of the [ordinary taxable income | working holiday taxable
-- income] of the taxpayer that:" / "exceeds $X but does not exceed $Y" / "The rate is:". One row per item. A part that "does not
-- exceed $Y" with no lower figure starts from $0; a part that "exceeds $X" with no upper figure has no upper limit (NOTHING).
DECLARE `Schedule 7 table` IS ONE OF
    -- Compilation No. 62 (C2024C00132), used for 2023-24
    `Part I, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
    `Part II, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
    `Part III, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
    -- Compilation No. 66 (C2026C00300)
    `Part I, for the 2024-25 or 2025-26 year of income`
    `Part I, for the 2026-27 year of income`
    `Part I, for the 2027-28 year of income or a later year of income`
    `Part II, for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income`
    `Part III, for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income`

-- The rows below are built with positional OF, so the ORDER of these fields is the order of the columns in every table.
DECLARE `Schedule 7 item` HAS
    `item`                      IS A NUMBER
    `for the part that exceeds` IS A NUMBER
    `but does not exceed`       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the rate is`               IS A NUMBER
    `table`                     IS A `Schedule 7 table`

-- Schedule 7 tables are MARGINAL: clause 1(b) applies "for each part of the ordinary taxable income specified in the table ...
-- the rate applicable under that table". So each item's rate bites only on the part inside its own band.
-- Clause 4 (Parts I and II alike): "(a) count the taxpayer's working holiday taxable income ... as the first parts (starting
-- from $0) of the taxpayer's ordinary taxable income for the purposes of the table in clause 1 ...; and (b) do not apply the
-- rates in that table to that working holiday taxable income". `the parts not taxed` is that working holiday taxable income
-- (0 where there is none): the part of the income in an item's band is the part above it.
GIVEN `the income`         IS A NUMBER
      `the parts not taxed` IS A NUMBER
      `the row`            IS A `Schedule 7 item`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax on the part of` `the income` `above` `the parts not taxed` `in the band of` `the row` MEANS
    `the part in the band` TIMES `the row`'s `the rate is`
    WHERE
        `the top of the part` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the row`'s `but does not exceed`
            WHEN NOTHING     THEN `the income`
            WHEN JUST `top`  THEN min `the income` `top`
        `the bottom of the part` MEANS
            max `the parts not taxed` (`the row`'s `for the part that exceeds`)
        `the part in the band` MEANS
            max 0 (`the top of the part` MINUS `the bottom of the part`)

GIVEN `the table`          IS A `Schedule 7 table`
      `the rows`           IS A LIST OF `Schedule 7 item`
      `the income`         IS A NUMBER
      `the parts not taxed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under` `the table` `of` `the rows` `on` `the income` `above` `the parts not taxed` MEANS
    sum (map `the tax in this row` (filter `a row of the table` `the rows`))
    WHERE
        `a row of the table` `row` MEANS `row`'s `table` EQUALS `the table`
        `the tax in this row` `row` MEANS
            `the tax on the part of` `the income` `above` `the parts not taxed` `in the band of` `row`

§§ `Schedule 7 Part I -- resident taxpayers`

-- Clause 1: "Subject to clauses 2, 3 and 4, the rates of tax on the taxable income of a resident taxpayer are as follows: (a)
-- 45% for the superannuation remainder (if any) of the taxable income; (aa) 45% for the employment termination remainder (if
-- any) of the taxable income; (b) for each part of the ordinary taxable income specified in the table applicable to the year of
-- income -- the rate applicable under that table."
-- Three tables only: "for the 2024-25 or 2025-26 year of income" (item 1: "exceeds the tax-free threshold but does not exceed
-- $45,000" -- 16%); "for the 2026-27 year of income" (15%); "for the 2027-28 year of income or a later year of income" (14%).
-- Items 2 to 4 are the same in all three: over $45,000 to $135,000 -- 30%; over $135,000 to $190,000 -- 37%; over $190,000 -- 45%.
-- Item 1 starts at "the tax-free threshold", which s 20(1) may replace: hence `the threshold` is a parameter of the table.
-- Compilation No. 62 adds, for 2023-24, "Tax rates for resident taxpayers for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of
-- income": item 1 "exceeds the tax-free threshold but does not exceed $45,000" 19%; item 2 "exceeds $45,000 but does not exceed
-- $120,000" 32.5%; item 3 "exceeds $120,000 but does not exceed $180,000" 37%; item 4 "exceeds $180,000" 45%.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) Schedule 7 Part I clause 1(b), the three tables; Compilation No. 62, the 2023-24 table
GIVEN `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Schedule 7 item`
`the Part I tables` MEANS
    --                         item exceeds          does not exceed the rate is table
    LIST (`Schedule 7 item` OF 1,   `the threshold`, JUST    45000,  19%,        `Part I, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`)
       , (^                 ^  2,   45000,           ^       120000, 32.5%,      ^)
       , (^                 ^  3,   120000,          ^       180000, 37%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  4,   180000,          NOTHING ,       45%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  1,   `the threshold`, JUST    45000,  16%,        `Part I, for the 2024-25 or 2025-26 year of income`)
       , (^                 ^  2,   45000,           ^       135000, 30%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  3,   135000,          ^       190000, 37%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  4,   190000,          NOTHING ,       45%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  1,   `the threshold`, JUST    45000,  15%,        `Part I, for the 2026-27 year of income`)
       , (^                 ^  2,   45000,           ^       135000, 30%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  3,   135000,          ^       190000, 37%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  4,   190000,          NOTHING ,       45%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  1,   `the threshold`, JUST    45000,  14%,        `Part I, for the 2027-28 year of income or a later year of income`)
       , (^                 ^  2,   45000,           ^       135000, 30%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  3,   135000,          ^       190000, 37%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  4,   190000,          NOTHING ,       45%,        ^)

-- Compilation No. 66 has no table for 2023-24 or earlier; Compilation No. 62 (deposited for REQ-0056) gives 2023-24. For
-- 2022-23 and earlier there is no deposited compilation in force for the year. That is not the law saying those years are
-- untaxed: their rates are in compilations not deposited. So the answer is `not covered`.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) Schedule 7 Part I clause 1(b), "the table applicable to the year of income" (2023-24 on)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Schedule 7 table`
`the Part I table applicable to the year of income` `the year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the year` EQUALS 2023
        THEN `answered` `Part I, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
        IF   (`the year` AT LEAST 2024) AND (`the year` AT MOST 2025)
        THEN `answered` `Part I, for the 2024-25 or 2025-26 year of income`
        IF   `the year` EQUALS 2026
        THEN `answered` `Part I, for the 2026-27 year of income`
        IF   `the year` AT LEAST 2027
        THEN `answered` `Part I, for the 2027-28 year of income or a later year of income`
        OTHERWISE `not covered` `the deposited compilations have no Schedule 7 table for a year of income before 2023-24`

-- s 3(1): "second resident personal tax rate means the rate mentioned in item 2 of the table in clause 1 of Part I of Schedule 7
-- that is applicable to the year of income"; "third resident personal tax rate" likewise, item 3.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 3(1), "second resident personal tax rate", "third resident personal tax rate"
GIVEN `the item`  IS A NUMBER
      `the table` IS A `Schedule 7 table`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate in item` `the item` `of Part I table` `the table` MEANS
    at (map `its rate` (filter `the item asked for` (`the Part I tables` `the tax-free threshold`))) 0
    WHERE
        `the item asked for` `row` MEANS
                `row`'s `table` EQUALS `the table`
            AND `row`'s `item`  EQUALS `the item`
        `its rate` `row` MEANS `row`'s `the rate is`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the second resident personal tax rate for` `the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` `the year`
    WHEN `answered` `the table`  THEN `answered` (`the rate in item` 2 `of Part I table` `the table`)
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the third resident personal tax rate for` `the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` `the year`
    WHEN `answered` `the table`  THEN `answered` (`the rate in item` 3 `of Part I table` `the table`)
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`

-- Convenience: the clause 1(b) tax of a resident with no remainders, no working holiday income and the full threshold.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) Schedule 7 Part I clause 1(b)
GIVEN `the income` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the resident tax on ordinary taxable income of` `the income` `for` `the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` `the year`
    WHEN `answered` `the table`
        THEN `answered` (`the tax under` `the table` `of` (`the Part I tables` `the tax-free threshold`) `on` `the income` `above` 0)
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`

§§ `Schedule 7 Part II -- non-resident taxpayers`

-- Clause 1 is Part I clause 1 with "non-resident taxpayer" for "resident taxpayer". One table, "for the 2024-25 year of income
-- or a later year of income": up to $135,000 -- "The second resident personal tax rate"; over $135,000 to $190,000 -- "The third
-- resident personal tax rate"; over $190,000 -- 45%. No tax-free threshold. The two named rates are parameters of the table,
-- supplied from s 3 for the year.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) Schedule 7 Part II clause 1(b), the table
GIVEN `the second resident personal tax rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the third resident personal tax rate`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Schedule 7 item`
`the Part II table` MEANS
    --                         item exceeds does not exceed the rate is                              table
    LIST (`Schedule 7 item` OF 1,   0,      JUST    135000, `the second resident personal tax rate`, `Part II, for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income`)
       , (^                 ^  2,   135000, ^       190000, `the third resident personal tax rate`,  ^)
       , (^                 ^  3,   190000, NOTHING ,       45%,                                     ^)

-- Compilation No. 62, "Tax rates for non-resident taxpayers for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income": item 1
-- "does not exceed $120,000 -- The second resident personal tax rate"; item 2 "exceeds $120,000 but does not exceed $180,000 --
-- 37%" (a plain figure, not "the third resident personal tax rate"); item 3 "exceeds $180,000 -- 45%".
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) Schedule 7 Part II clause 1(b), Compilation No. 62, the 2023-24 table
GIVEN `the second resident personal tax rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Schedule 7 item`
`the Part II table for 2023-24` MEANS
    --                         item exceeds does not exceed the rate is                              table
    LIST (`Schedule 7 item` OF 1,   0,      JUST    120000, `the second resident personal tax rate`, `Part II, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`)
       , (^                 ^  2,   120000, ^       180000, 37%,                                     ^)
       , (^                 ^  3,   180000, NOTHING ,       45%,                                     ^)

-- The rows of whichever Part II table applies, with the s 3 rates for the year.
GIVEN `the table` IS A `Schedule 7 table`
      `the second resident personal tax rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the third resident personal tax rate`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Schedule 7 item`
`the rows of the Part II table` `the table` `with` `the second resident personal tax rate` `and` `the third resident personal tax rate` MEANS
    IF   `the table` EQUALS `Part II, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
    THEN `the Part II table for 2023-24` `the second resident personal tax rate`
    ELSE `the Part II table` `the second resident personal tax rate` `the third resident personal tax rate`

@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) Schedule 7 Part II clause 1(b)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Schedule 7 table`
`the Part II table applicable to the year of income` `the year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the year` EQUALS 2023
        THEN `answered` `Part II, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
        IF   `the year` AT LEAST 2024
        THEN `answered` `Part II, for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income`
        OTHERWISE `not covered` `the deposited compilations have no Schedule 7 table for a year of income before 2023-24`

§§ `Schedule 7 Part III -- working holiday makers`

-- Clause 1: "The rates of tax on a taxpayer's working holiday taxable income for a year of income are as set out in the table
-- that is applicable to the year of income." "Tax rates for working holiday makers for the 2024-25 year of income or a later
-- year of income": up to $45,000 -- 15%; over $45,000 to $135,000 -- 30%; over $135,000 to $190,000 -- 37%; over $190,000 -- 45%.
-- (s 3A: a working holiday maker holds a Subclass 417 or 462 visa, a qualifying bridging visa or a COVID-19 pandemic event 408
-- visa.) Compilation No. 62, "Tax rates for working holiday makers for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of
-- income": up to $45,000 -- 15%; over $45,000 to $120,000 -- 32.5%; over $120,000 to $180,000 -- 37%; over $180,000 -- 45%.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) Schedule 7 Part III clause 1, the table; Compilation No. 62, the 2023-24 table
GIVETH A LIST OF `Schedule 7 item`
`the Part III table` MEANS
    --                         item exceeds does not exceed the rate is table
    LIST (`Schedule 7 item` OF 1,   0,      JUST    45000,  15%,        `Part III, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`)
       , (^                 ^  2,   45000,  ^       120000, 32.5%,      ^)
       , (^                 ^  3,   120000, ^       180000, 37%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  4,   180000, NOTHING ,       45%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  1,   0,      JUST    45000,  15%,        `Part III, for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income`)
       , (^                 ^  2,   45000,  ^       135000, 30%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  3,   135000, ^       190000, 37%,        ^)
       , (^                 ^  4,   190000, NOTHING ,       45%,        ^)

@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) Schedule 7 Part III clause 1
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Schedule 7 table`
`the Part III table applicable to the year of income` `the year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the year` EQUALS 2023
        THEN `answered` `Part III, for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income`
        IF   `the year` AT LEAST 2024
        THEN `answered` `Part III, for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income`
        OTHERWISE `not covered` `the deposited compilations have no Schedule 7 table for a year of income before 2023-24`

§§ `Schedule 7 -- putting it together`

-- Clauses 2 and 3 of Parts I and II (a special income component: abnormal income averaging) displace clause 1 -- "Subject to
-- clauses 2, 3 and 4" -- and their formula is not in the deposit. The answer is `not covered`, not an answer under clause 1.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) Schedule 7 Part I clause 1(b), Part II clause 1(b), clause 4 of each
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`clause 1(b), the table tax on the ordinary taxable income of` `p` MEANS
    IF   `a resident taxpayer` `p`
    THEN CONSIDER `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` `the year`
         WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
         WHEN `answered` `the table` THEN
             CONSIDER `the tax-free threshold that applies to` `p`
             WHEN `not covered` `the gap`    THEN `not covered` `the gap`
             WHEN `answered` `the threshold` THEN
                 `answered` (`the tax under` `the table`
                                 `of` (`the Part I tables` `the threshold`)
                                 `on` (`the ordinary taxable income of` `p`) `above` (`p`'s `working holiday taxable income`))
    ELSE CONSIDER `the Part II table applicable to the year of income` `the year`
         WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
         WHEN `answered` `the table` THEN
             CONSIDER `the Part I table applicable to the year of income` `the year`
             WHEN `not covered` `the gap`         THEN `not covered` `the gap`
             WHEN `answered` `the Part I table`   THEN
                 `answered` (`the tax under` `the table`
                                 `of` (`the rows of the Part II table` `the table`
                                          `with` (`the rate in item` 2 `of Part I table` `the Part I table`)
                                          `and`  (`the rate in item` 3 `of Part I table` `the Part I table`))
                                 `on` (`the ordinary taxable income of` `p`) `above` (`p`'s `working holiday taxable income`))
    WHERE
        `the year` MEANS `p`'s `year of income begins`

@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 12(1); Schedule 7 Part I clauses 1-3, Part II clauses 1-3, Part III clause 1
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the tax under Schedule 7 on the taxable income of` `p` MEANS
    IF   `p`'s `taxable income includes a special income component`
    THEN `not covered` `Schedule 7 clauses 2 and 3 (a special income component) are not encoded: their formula is not in the deposited compilation`
    ELSE CONSIDER `clause 1(b), the table tax on the ordinary taxable income of` `p`
         WHEN `not covered` `the gap`    THEN `not covered` `the gap`
         WHEN `answered` `the table tax` THEN
             CONSIDER `the Part III table applicable to the year of income` (`p`'s `year of income begins`)
             WHEN `not covered` `the gap`         THEN `not covered` `the gap`
             WHEN `answered` `the Part III table that applies` THEN
                 `answered` (     (45% TIMES `p`'s `superannuation remainder`)          -- clause 1(a)
                             PLUS (45% TIMES `p`'s `employment termination remainder`)  -- clause 1(aa)
                             PLUS `the table tax`                                       -- clause 1(b), clause 4
                             PLUS (`the tax under` `the Part III table that applies`    -- Part III
                                       `of` `the Part III table`
                                       `on` (`p`'s `working holiday taxable income`) `above` 0))

§§ `s 23AA -- base rate entity`

-- s 23(1): "The rates of tax payable by a company, other than a company in the capacity of a trustee, are as set out in the
-- following provisions of this section." s 23(2) applies "if subsections (3) to (5) and section 23A do not apply to the
-- company"; s 23(7) caps the tax of "a recognised medium credit union". So the kinds of company s 23 tells apart:
DECLARE `Kind of company` IS ONE OF
    `a company to which none of s 23(3) to (5), s 23(7) or s 23A applies`
    `an RSA provider`                          -- s 23(3)
    `a PDF`                                    -- s 23(4), (5)
    `a life insurance company`                 -- s 23A
    `a recognised medium credit union`         -- s 23(7)
    `a company in the capacity of a trustee`   -- s 23(1)

DECLARE Company HAS
    `year of income begins`           IS A NUMBER
    `kind`                            IS A `Kind of company`
    `assessable income`               IS A NUMBER
    `base rate entity passive income` IS A NUMBER
    `aggregated turnover`             IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income`                  IS A NUMBER
    `a non-profit company`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- "An entity is a base rate entity for a year of income if: (a) no more than 80% of its assessable income for the year of
-- income is base rate entity passive income; and (b) its aggregated turnover (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment
-- Act 1997) for the year of income, worked out as at the end of that year, is less than $50 million."
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 23AA(a), (b)
GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a base rate entity` `c` MEANS
        "(a)" ... `c`'s `base rate entity passive income` AT MOST 80% TIMES `c`'s `assessable income`
    AND "(b)" ... `c`'s `aggregated turnover` LESS THAN 50000000

§§ `s 23(2) -- the company rate`

-- s 23(2): "The rate of tax in respect of the taxable income of a company is: (a) if the company is a base rate entity for a year
-- of income -- 25%; or (b) otherwise -- 30%; if subsections (3) to (5) and section 23A do not apply to the company."
-- Unlike Schedule 7, s 23 names no year of income. The compilation is the law as at 1 July 2026, and nothing in it says from
-- which year 25% and 30% apply (earlier years had other rates, set by earlier compilations). So the encoding answers only for
-- the years from which the deposited compilation's own tables run, 2024-25 on -- the encoder's boundary, not the Act's.
-- So a company's year of income before 2024-25 is answered `not covered`, and so are the kinds of company whose rate s 23(2)
-- does not give.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 23(1), (2); s 23(3)-(5) and s 23A, and s 12(6) with Schedule 10, are not encoded
GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the s 23(2) rate of tax on the taxable income of` `c` MEANS
    IF   `c`'s `year of income begins` LESS THAN 2024
    THEN `not covered` `this encoding states no company rate for a year of income before 2024-25`
    ELSE CONSIDER `c`'s `kind`
         WHEN `a company in the capacity of a trustee` THEN `not covered` `s 23 does not give the rate for a company in the capacity of a trustee, and the rate that does is not encoded`
         WHEN `an RSA provider`                        THEN `not covered` `the rates in s 23(3) to (5) and s 23A (RSA providers, PDFs, life insurance companies) are not encoded`
         WHEN `a PDF`                                  THEN `not covered` `the rates in s 23(3) to (5) and s 23A (RSA providers, PDFs, life insurance companies) are not encoded`
         WHEN `a life insurance company`               THEN `not covered` `the rates in s 23(3) to (5) and s 23A (RSA providers, PDFs, life insurance companies) are not encoded`
         OTHERWISE
             BRANCH
                 IF        `a base rate entity` `c` THEN `answered` (25%)  -- (a)
                 OTHERWISE                              `answered` (30%)  -- (b)

§§ `s 23(6) -- non-profit companies`

-- s 23(6): "The amount of tax payable by a company (before applying any ... tax offset ...) must not be greater than 55% of the
-- amount (if any) by which the taxable income of the company exceeds $416, if: (a) the company is a non-profit company; and (b)
-- the taxable income is not greater than: (i) if the company is a base rate entity for a year of income -- $762; or (ii)
-- otherwise -- $915." The "must not be greater than" is a ceiling on an amount, not a duty on anyone: a min, not a MUST.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 23(6)(b)(i), (ii)
GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 23(6)(b) limit for` `c` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF        `a base rate entity` `c` THEN 762    -- (i)
        OTHERWISE                              915    -- (ii)

@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 23(6)(a), (b)
GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(6) applies to` `c` MEANS
        "(a)" ... `c`'s `a non-profit company`
    AND "(b)" ... `c`'s `taxable income` AT MOST `the s 23(6)(b) limit for` `c`

@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 23(6)
GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 23(6) ceiling for` `c` MEANS
    55% TIMES max 0 (`c`'s `taxable income` MINUS 416)

-- s 23(7) caps the tax of a recognised medium credit union. It is not encoded, so that company's tax is `not covered`.
@ref Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) s 23(2), (6), (7)
GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the tax payable by the company before offsets` `c` MEANS
    IF   `c`'s `kind` EQUALS `a recognised medium credit union`
    THEN `not covered` `the s 23(7) ceiling for a recognised medium credit union is not encoded`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the s 23(2) rate of tax on the taxable income of` `c`
         WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
         WHEN `answered` `the rate`   THEN
             IF   `s 23(6) applies to` `c`
             THEN `answered` (min (`c`'s `taxable income` TIMES `the rate`) (`the s 23(6) ceiling for` `c`))
             ELSE `answered` (`c`'s `taxable income` TIMES `the rate`)
